  "implemented": [
    "Organization and personal navigation use one tenant catalog; no stored mode, platform fallback or managed/platform merge; alias expiry is rechecked against the tenant graph",
    "Managed registration resolves parent and host within the ready tenant directory; tenant-qualified code/path conflicts, fresh tenant locking and owner namespace remain enforced",
    "Tenant host availability, applicable scope, page type, executable component and dependency hierarchy gate authorization and activation; host grants are never implicitly added",
    "Generated navigation resolves the current tenant host component without rewriting immutable publication metadata",
    "Tenant and personal administrators cannot use hasRole alternatives or inherited schema to bypass missing tenant entitlements; shared domain-owned endpoints retain their own data policy boundary",
    "Explicit application membership and package acquisition include non-grantable executable capabilities such as hidden hosts; no role grant or public access is invented; current time balance still gates use"
